WEBVTT

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.390
Not a hallucination?

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.260
I'm convinced that that space was actually altered.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.660
You're trying to say it was a physical phenomenon?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.470
With their power, it might be possible.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:10.570
Pardon me.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.210
How is Tatsuya?

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:18.380
I gave him a sedative, but he still appears to be quite agitated.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.810
Shall I bring him here, my lady?

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:26.420
Better to leave him alone. But don't let him out of your sight.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:35.960
Certainly... Certainly manipulating nearby molecules could be a simple matter for them.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:39.970
Or constructing a separate space within a barrier field.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:46.400
If we assume that was a physical phenomenon, there's also a possibility that clues were left.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.850
Find anything?

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.180
Nothing, no sign at all of where they escaped to.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.290
I see. That's good enough. Tell Fuko too.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.320
Would you make a request to the manager for me?

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:05.860
Ask him if he'll search for mistakes for us.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:13.060
Nothing seems to be different.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:21.950
Show me.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:23.440
Yes, Sir.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.120
As I thought...

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.610
Yes...

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:28.690
You see something?

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.810
Please look at the relief on the column.

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:34.450
It had a cleaner symmetry.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.030
Take a look and compare, my lady.

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.560
It's subtly unbalanced, isn't it? I'm amazed you realized that.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:48.000
I'm quite attached to this building. But why did something like this...

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:54.110
I beg your pardon, but may I scrape a bit off of here?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.980
Now I understand your reasoning.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.520
If we suppose that when that space changed,

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:08.250
...they also used molecules of their own which coat the anti-matter,

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:12.220
...it would not be odd if a portion of them were left behind.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.330
This is also a supposition,

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:18.030
...but if they exchange their coating molecules over a fixed time period...

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.530
...in a metabolic sort of process,

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.970
...that would serve as a basis for inferring what their surroundings are.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:28.910
So if you find a clue in that, you'll go looking for them.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:45.360
As I thought, there is something. Titanium, and premium grade at that.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.960
What's that?

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.870
If it's premium grade, its uses are limited.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.870
The majority of it is used in flaps and turbine blades on aircraft.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.000
If so, that means airports and such?

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:04.000
I think pursuing this along those lines would be the surest way.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.450
Around here, the number of places is limited too.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.060
Did you figure it out?

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.460
Doesn't it look close to this?

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.420
Yeah...

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.790
A black-tailed gull...

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:43.080
We're thinking of going out for a bit.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.380
To pick up Kiyoko.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.060
Huh?

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:49.390
Are you coming? Or will you wait here?

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:54.530
I'll go with you.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:57.260
Then you're one of us, just for today at least.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.630
I'll put some Dynamis into you, so you don't get lost.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.240
You'll be fine. I'll only put in a little.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.050
Relax your mind, maintain a feeling of accepting everything that comes.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:12.200
Hey, don't fight; there's plenty. There!

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:40.700
Sorry to bring you to this kind of place.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.540
Actually, it'd be better if your brother were with you,

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.880
...but we'll be sure to take care of that soon.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:51.950
There's a single reason why we've asked you here against your will.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.180
Before long, the Professor will go back into action.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.190
It's a very ambitious project,

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:02.150
...and we need your strength and your brother's for it!

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.660
First of all, won't you see the Professor?

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:13.000
Then we want you to work with us, to restore peace and order to this universe.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:25.240
To restore the universe's peace and order?

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.480
Well, that's splendid self-promotion anyway!

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:33.790
I didn't think Dad would stoop so low,

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:36.060
...since he's made an enemy of the entire world anyway.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:39.990
To carry out a plan, in some cases you use these sorts of methods.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.100
They're necessary measures!

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:46.500
No, this is just a base kidnapping... the worst kind.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.040
Hey!

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.300
This, I should tell you, is something we thought to do ourselves.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.110
It's not that we received a direct order.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:58.140
The Professor really wanted to see the two of you though.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.650
What's that about, after all this time?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.720
Conquer the world, destroy the Earth...

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.850
Dad can do just as he pleases.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:10.260
He can go ahead and do as he likes. But leave us alone!

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.890
Is there anything as cruel as this?

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:18.130
Always, everywhere, that mirror is looking down on us.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:24.470
We can't escape from the crime our father committed.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.010
The mirror's denser, somehow.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:46.190
Then you have no intention of seeing the Professor?

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.190
No.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:50.890
I wonder how Tatsuya feels about it?

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.960
He feels the same.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.130
I can't believe that.

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.570
What do you know?

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.980
We can take just YOU to him by force, you know!

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:07.250
If you do anything like that...

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:09.150
Do you want to die?

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:19.590
Novem...

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:26.500
Sorry to bring you here. We're done now.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:31.400
You're free to leave. We're releasing you.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:33.480
I'd like to lead you out,

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.570
...but Tatsuya and the others are here to pick you up.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:40.820
You have my word, we won't do this a second time.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:45.390
But if you should stand in our way after this, you're an enemy...

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:49.320
...and we'll give no quarter then. This is the Professor's will.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.730
Tell that to Tatsuya too!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.490
His will? Did he say that by telepathy or something?

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.470
How convenient.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:01.170
No, the Professor is everywhere, in all of creation,

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:05.730
...and he is conveying his will to you and to us even now.

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:08.140
Listen...

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:13.880
I've heard you were very sensitive to sound when you were little.

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:19.140
I guess it's not this airport.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:21.310
Yeah...

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:27.550
Kiyoko!

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:30.120
Tatsuya...

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.960
You're okay?

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.950
Huh? Yeah...

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.790
I sense a terrible malice here.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.700
Get away. Quickly!

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.570
Let's stop running. It's all the same.

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:32.970
It's not like we can escape from this sky anyway.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.250
Kiyoko...

00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:40.990
Dad is probably watching too.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:42.780
What does that mean?

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.900
It's somehow as if we're in a bad dream that goes on and on.

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:10.410
When we wake up, there will be a real world, and the real us.

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:16.090
I wonder what we're doing there? You're a pianist.

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:21.620
I don't have the talent. I'm probably a piano tuner.

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:24.430
A piano tuner? Like that guy yesterday?

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:30.090
Yeah, and I go to concert halls around the world with a maestro.

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.240
Huh...

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.000
That's been my dream.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.200
I had a dream about right now.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:55.020
In the dream, I was running away with you, chased by Gilgamesh.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:24.050
Get in the car.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:34.300
Quickly! The dust is going to get in.

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:48.040
You're a nonchalant pair, moving so leisurely at a time like this.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.390
Don't come!

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:58.340
Isamu!

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:04.880
You can hear me, right? Capture it alive!

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.270
Look out! Isamu!

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.330
It seems one of the creatures has died.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.500
I'll have you take the time to tell me all about it later.

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:08.010
I imagine it was hard on you, but plan on talking about it.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:26.330
The smoke and its reflection make a single line.

00:23:25.150 --> 00:23:26.950
Family is an irreplaceable thing.

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:30.320
Though admittedly temporary, we're a family too.

00:23:30.320 --> 00:23:32.220
I was thinking of you when I did this.

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:34.590
Your life was nothing but running away, with your little brother.

00:23:34.590 --> 00:23:38.960
I wonder if you might not be enraptured by kind words spoken by a good-looking boy?

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:44.370
I'm still suspicious about whether you went with them of your own will.

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:46.500
He's beginning to accept his own destiny.

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:49.340
I'm very aware that I'm willfully having my own say,

00:23:49.340 --> 00:23:50.870
...but let me say just one thing.

00:23:50.870 --> 00:23:53.430
Just do not get in our way.
